n: 3.9
name: in-language-emitter
kind: hub
is: Only jit-page.bml (396 lines) is offered by the runtime's heat, at 4096 calls: it compiles node by node, keeps the walker's tagged word and frame, calls a 38-word helper table numbered ABI 4 and hands uncovered nodes back to the walker. Recorded gain: about 20x on a tight int loop, 1.6x on compiler work. No wrong answer of the page is on record; a page is never unbound. form-macho.fk writes a 251-byte unsigned object that needs the system linker.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.1
name: writers
kind: hub
is: Five writers of machine code or code text stand in the old body's own language beside the C loop lane. Only the 396-line page emitter is offered by the runtime's heat; the leaf compiler runs by explicit call or through a heat gate kept in Form, the CPU images by explicit call, and the C lane fires first at 1024 calls. Two doors of the runtime accept raw machine bytes with no content check.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.1.2
name: heat-wiring
kind: observation
is: Of the in-language writers the runtime's heat offers only the page emitter, at every 4096th call of a defn or 32nd time sample; the leaf compiler has its own heat count in Form and CPU images run by explicit call. The C loop lane (380 hex-word sites) fires at 1024 calls; the page offer skips a body wearing tag 194, which a bound page wears too.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#10281 2.1.7#10296-10299 2.1.7#24094 2.1.7#24350 2.1.7#1034 2.1.7#31791-31792 2.1.7#10518 2.1.6#1381-1382 2.17.7#47 2.17.6#16-17 2.17.21#16-21
see: 3.9.1.4
limit: The 380 is a count of lines matching fk_f64_put(words, wn, 0x in the runtime file. The C loop lane itself was not read by the reading. The leaf compiler's heat count is a gate in Form that a program must call (3.9.1.4); the runtime's pulse knows nothing of it.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.1.4
name: leaf-heat-gate
kind: observation
is: The leaf compiler is not offered by the runtime. A gate in Form, jit-heat-gate.fk, counts requests per program identity at its door, answers through the interpreter below the mark, and compiles once through the leaf compiler when a lowerable program's count reaches 5; a program reaches it only by calling the gate.
status: observed
src: 2.17.21#16-21 2.17.21#39-46 2.17.21#65-78 2.17.21#79-92 2.17.22#98 2.17.22#109 2.17.22#119-133 2.17.23#14-16 2.17.7#49-56
limit: Read, not run. Lowerable means every row is a literal, the argument, add, sub, mul or a division by a nonzero literal. The cool step halves every count and drops an entry whose count falls below 2 from the registry it threads; it does not call the door's release, which jit-once-born.fk sends only from its sweep on a new epoch or a changed image. Callers found by search: form-cli-jit.bml, rest-force-jit.fk and two tests.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2
name: page
kind: hub
is: jit-page.bml is a partial compiler that works node by node and never refuses a defn for holding a node it cannot say. By the reading's count it handles about 55 node kinds and writes instructions for the int path of 28; the rest go to the walker's own C functions. Floats, closures, indirect calls, attempt and record_new stay walked. Values stay the walker's tagged words in the walker's frame.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2.1
name: own-words
kind: observation
is: jit-page.bml writes with no helper call: int literals below 2^61, nil, a pinned string literal's word, parameter and let reads, let, do, and behind an int test the int paths of add sub mul div mod, band bor bxor, le lt eq and five u32 ops. An if reads condition words 0 and 2 in place and calls the truth helper (table word 3) for any other word.
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#134-143 2.1.14#173-206 2.1.14#234-238 2.1.14#256-277
limit: The int test is orr then tbnz bit 0, and tbnz alone for the one-operand bnot_u32 (line 237). A non-int operand or a zero divisor calls the op's helper, except that an eq with a nil side is answered in page words (line 263).
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2.2
name: calls
kind: observation
is: In jit-page.bml a self tail call becomes a loop: arguments go to temporaries, move to the parameter slots, the deadline tick helper runs, then a branch back. A callee whose tail spine makes no call is written in place of its call, two deep and up to 768 words. Any other call evaluates arguments left to right into slots and calls helper 6 or 7.
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#299-370 2.1.14#373
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2.3
name: mirror
kind: observation
is: For a node with no arm of its own, jit-page.bml asks the runtime door jit_node for the node's value children, evaluates each into a frame temporary, has the runtime mint a new walker node whose children read those slots, and has the walker run only that node. Which nodes may be split this way is a table in C beside the walker (fk_jit_plain_kids).
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#144-172 2.1.7#10535-10546 2.17.13#23
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2.4
name: declines-and-handoff
kind: observation
is: A node jit-page.bml cannot say is walked in place in value position or in tail position handed back through the table's next cell to the walker in the same frame. A whole defn is declined if no node was taken in page words, the frame needs over 4095 slots or has no readable slot count, the offer is malformed or not ABI 4, or the bind door refuses.
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#104-107 2.1.14#114 2.1.14#379 2.1.14#384 2.1.14#388-393 2.1.7#10456-10482 2.1.7#11065-11078
limit: A malformed offer is nothing or a list of fewer than four items (line 390). The bind door refuses a value that names no defn, a defn already bound, words not headed by ABI 4, a word outside 0 to 2^32-1, an empty word list, and everything on a host other than Darwin arm64.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2.5
name: registers-and-frame
kind: observation
is: A page is entered as page(fp, table). x19 holds the helper table, x20 the frame index, x21 the frame's address, recomputed after every helper call because a helper can grow the value stack; x0 holds the current value. Parameters, lets and the page's temporaries are all value-stack cells, so no value lives in a register across a helper call.
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#10-13 2.1.14#97-100 2.1.14#374-383 2.1.7#10249
limit: That a stop raised inside a helper unwinds safely over a page's native frame is inferred by the reading from this convention; the recover point's restore was not read against the in-place frame-chain push.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.2.6
name: tagged-word-in-code
kind: observation
is: Page code uses the walker's value word unchanged: an int n is the even word 2n, a compare answers 0 or 2, nil is the word 1; pairs, strings and floats are odd words that page code never builds or opens. Node ids, defn ids and pinned string words stand in the code as immediates, so a page is valid only in the process that made it.
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#104-108 2.1.14#137-143 2.1.14#257-263 2.1.7#15386-15393 2.17.14#50-53
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.3
name: host-contract
kind: hub
is: The page's contract with the C runtime is a 38-word helper table numbered ABI 4, a bind door, a node-reading door and the mirror door. A defn is offered at a heat or time mark to the emitter running as a cell in the same process. A bound page is never released, a failing offer stops the user's program, and a decline carries no reason. The reading derives a replacement of ten functions and one callback.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.3.1
name: helper-table
kind: observation
is: Page code calls the runtime through one static 38-word table, ABI 4: stack base, next node, walk, truth, tick, enter, call, tail, 26 operations shared with the walker's arms, and 4 frame-chain words (3 addresses and a capacity number). Every offer carries the number; the emitter declines another and the bind door refuses words not headed by it.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#10250-10280 2.1.7#10470 2.1.7#10498-10516 2.1.7#15410-15411 2.1.7#15565-15572 2.1.7#31793 2.1.14#92-96 2.1.14#388-393
limit: The three addresses are of the running defn, of the chain's depth and of the chain array; the fourth word, fr_cap, is the chain's capacity FK_FR_CAP as a number (lines 10275-10278, 10512-10515). Nine of the 26 operations, eight bit ops and value_kind, are one-line wrappers over a function that the walker's code calls at lines 21008 and 21318.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.3.2
name: offer-and-queue
kind: observation
is: The runtime offers a defn when its call count reaches a nonzero multiple of 4096, or when the sampler has posted 32 time samples for a never-offered defn. The offer runs jit-page.bml as a cell in the same process with [defn, body, arity, 4]. While the emitter is busy a defn waits once in a line of 64. FK_NO_JIT turns the lane off.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#10281-10300 2.1.7#31730 2.1.7#31788-31793 2.1.7#31838-31854
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.3.3
name: bind-and-no-release
kind: observation
is: jit_fn_bind checks the defn, that no page stands, the ABI head and that every word is an int in 0 to 2^32-1, then maps the words and replaces the defn's body by a node (194, defn, old body). It binds only on Darwin arm64. Nothing unbinds or unmaps a page: lowering one unit bound 160 pages, each at least 16,384 bytes mapped, 2,621,440 bytes in all.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#10453-10522 2.1.6#1346
limit: The absence of an unbind rests on a search of the runtime file for assignments to the page table. The byte total is arithmetic from the floor record's 160 pages and this machine's page size, not a measurement.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.3.4
name: failure-and-refusals
kind: observation
is: If the emitter stops during an offer, the runtime writes a native-failure diagnostic and raises a stop in the program that crossed the heat mark. A declined defn is value 0 with no reason: a note of 2026-10-11 records every offer declined that way while the emitter's imports were not found. Only the jit_node door keeps a reason code, 1 to 10.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#31807-31818 2.1.14#389-393 2.1.7#10644-10649
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.3.5
name: proposed-interface
kind: finding
is: The reading proposes an emitter interface for a C bootstrap: ten functions (reserve, commit, release code; bind, unbind, query a recipe; the helper table; read a cell, a recipe's shape, an operation's row) and one callback, emit, whose failure is a counted decline with a reason. The table is per activation, numbered in word 0, literals by index.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.3.1 3.9.3.2 3.9.3.3 3.9.3.4 3.9.2.3 3.9.2.6
conf: mid
limit: A proposal: nothing of it was built or run, and the names are the reading's. It assumes a first tier on the interpreter's frame and tagged word; unboxed registers, saved native code and an executable-file writer lie outside it.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.4
name: encoders
kind: hub
is: Neither has labels, a register allocator or relocations. form-lower.fk compiles small integer trees in 32-bit registers; form-macho.fk writes an unsigned object file only. A probe confirmed 47 words and the object layout.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.4.1
name: page-encoders
kind: observation
is: jit-page.bml holds its own instruction table: 33 parametrized forms and 8 fixed words. Each form is a function answering base + field * 2^position, the base a decimal literal with the hex in a comment, for example jp-ldr = 4181721088 + slot * 1024 + rn * 32 + rt (f9400000). The file imports only core.fk; form-asm.fk line 183 repeats the same base.
status: observed
src: 2.1.14#30 2.1.14#41-102 2.1.14#110-111 2.1.14#369-373 2.17.2#183
limit: There are no general labels: branch distances are computed from list lengths at each site. The one fixup is the self tail call's branch, written as the placeholder word -1 and replaced by jp-link with a backward branch when the page is assembled.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.4.2
name: asm-rows
kind: observation
is: A comment says every word of the floating-point rows was verified byte for byte against clang's output.
status: observed
src: 2.17.2#26-35 2.17.2#40 2.17.2#215-216 2.17.2#301-304
limit: The verification claim is the file's own comment; the reading did not rerun it.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.4.3
name: leaf-compiler
kind: observation
is: form-lower.fk compiles a small tree in its own tag space to AAPCS64 code. It computes in 32-bit registers and sign-extends the result, so f(2000000000) answers 1705032711 where the walker answers 6000000007. A piece it cannot lower is nothing(), carried upward by lo-app. By its comments, compiled bytes cannot call back into the runtime.
status: observed
src: 2.17.3#32-35 2.17.3#243-254 2.17.3#414-423 2.17.12#13-15
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.4.4
name: anf-rows
kind: observation
is: anf-lower.bml turns a defn's nodes into rows in which every call's arguments are bound to temporaries in order before the call row, so a lowering has no argument expression left to substitute or drop. A defn holding an unknown node, a closure or a short-circuit operator answers nothing() whole, and anf-why names the node and the reason.
status: observed
src: 2.17.5#1-16
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.4.6
name: transcription-probe
kind: finding
is: The reading transcribed 39 sample encodings and the 8 fixed words of jit-page.bml into a C probe; Apple's otool decoded each to the instruction its comment names. A 251-byte object rebuilt from form-macho.fk's layout linked with ld (one warning), ran with exit status 40 and carried an ad-hoc linker signature.
status: assumed
limit: The probe checks the reading's transcription of the recipes' arithmetic against Apple's tools on one machine; the recipes themselves were not run, and the probe sat in a session scratch directory.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.5
name: speeds-and-faults
kind: hub
is: On record the page lane is about 20 times the walker on a tight int loop and about 1.6 times on compiler work; the C loop lane reaches about 60 times on a loop. The reading measured none of these. No wrong answer is recorded for jit-page.bml; recorded miscompiles belong to the C loop lane, to form-lower.fk, or to a second copy of an operation that drifted from the first. A fault of 2026-11-24 at call 1024 is open.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.5.1
name: page-speeds
kind: observation
is: The old body's floor record gives, walker against pages: a 3-million-step tail loop 156 ms against 7 ms, fingerprinting 232 KB 36 ms against 2 ms, lowering form-find.bml 2.1 s against 1.26 s and form-path.bml 1.65 s against 1.0 s. Lowering form-find made 171 offers, bound 160 pages and spent 0.15 s offering, about 0.9 ms an offer.
status: observed
src: 2.1.6#1339-1346
limit: The numbers are the record's own, dated 2026-10-11 by the reading, on one machine.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.5.3
name: second-copy-faults
kind: observation
is: Recorded wrong answers outside the page: the C loop lane inlined callees by substituting argument expressions, so past 1024 calls a plain build landed 3,936 of 780,000 effects (found 2026-10-03, guarded in C). In a former Go sibling kernel len answered 311 cold and 310 hot, because the primitive existed twice and one copy was healed (2026-07-17).
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#14728-14732
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.5.4
name: leaf-compiler-faults
kind: observation
is: form-lower.fk's comments record past wrong answers: an unsigned divide answered 2147483644 for -7/2; an uncovered tag lowered to an empty list and the image answered with a node missing; -3 arrived as 4294967293 before sign extension; a cond over a non-compare compared garbage registers; x19 to x22 were used unsaved. Each is described as fixed.
status: observed
