n: 3.9.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Seven things the reading would carry into a new emitter: per-node fallback to the interpreter; the interpreter's frame as the compiled frame; one definition per operation; a numbered helper table whose number travels both ways; arguments bound once in order, with a decline carried as nothing; encodings as checked data rows; and a cold-equals-hot check with a board that shows where compiled code is absent.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.1
name: per-node-fallback
kind: finding
is: Keep fallback per node instead of refusal per defn: a walk(node, frame) helper and a hand-off cell let an emitter start with about ten node kinds and grow one arm at a time, with the uncovered share measured by node kind. The 396-line page emitter was usable on compiler work with this design.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.2.4 3.9.2.1 3.9.5.1
conf: high
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.2
name: interpreter-frame
kind: finding
is: Keep the interpreter's frame as the compiled code's frame: every live value in a frame cell across any call out, and the frame address reloaded after every helper. A moving collector then needs no stack maps and no register roots. A self tail call becomes a loop that still ticks the deadline.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.2.5 3.9.2.2
conf: high
limit: Every temporary is then a memory slot. The recorded gain of this design is about 1.6 times on compiler work against about 60 times for untagged registers on a loop, and no measurement separates helper cost from slot traffic.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.3
name: one-definition-per-operation
kind: finding
is: Keep one definition per operation, called by the interpreter's arm and by compiled code's slow path, compiled code adding only an inline fast path behind a tag test. Recorded wrong answers after a heat mark whose cause is known came from a drifted second copy of a meaning; the fault of 2026-11-24 also appears at a heat mark, its cause unknown.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.3.1 3.9.2.1 3.9.5.3 3.9.5.5
conf: high
limit: The known-cause cases are those of 3.9.5.3. The reading's own table lists the 2026-11-24 fault (3.9.5.5) with root cause not known and marks the shared pattern as inferred, so that fault does not yet support the rule.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.4
name: numbered-helper-table
kind: finding
is: Keep a numbered helper table whose number is handed out with each offer and comes back in the bind, so an emitter written for one layout never binds code against another. The runtime's stated reason: a checked-out binary is not rebuilt by a merge, so emitter and runtime can differ in age.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.3.1
conf: high
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.5
name: ordered-temporaries-and-nothing
kind: finding
is: Keep argument order as a property of the intermediate form: every call's arguments bound once, in order, to temporaries before the call. Keep a decline as nothing carried upward, never an empty or partial image; the leaf compiler answered wrongly with full confidence while absence was an empty list.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.4.4 3.9.4.3 3.9.5.4 3.9.5.3 1.9.1
conf: high
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.6
name: encoding-rows-checked
kind: finding
is: Keep instruction encodings as data rows, a base and field multipliers through one packer, in one table for every writer, each row checked once against an outside assembler.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.4.2 3.9.4.6 3.9.4.1
conf: high
limit: The 80 and the 58 are wc -l and a reading of the reading's probe file gen.c in a session scratch directory on 2026-11-24; the file is kept in no repository.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.9.8.7
name: cold-equals-hot-check
kind: finding
is: Keep a cold-equals-hot check over the whole vocabulary that compares through the printed value, and the rule that output bytes are the same with the emitter off. Keep offering by time as well as by call count, with a board that names where compiled code is absent.
status: inferred
from: 3.9.5.6 3.9.3.2
conf: high
